//
// *** This is instruction selection, not machine code emission. ***
// Despite naming similarity, this module is unrelated to `trust-cg-codegen/lower.rs`.
// The two modules operate at opposite ends of the compilation pipeline:
//
//   trust-cg-lower/isel.rs   (Phase 1): trust_ir SSA IR  -> AArch64 MachIR (VRegs)
//   trust-cg-codegen/lower.rs (Phase 8): AArch64 MachIR (PRegs) -> binary bytes
//
// This module matches trust_ir opcodes to AArch64 instructions with virtual registers.
// `lower.rs` encodes already-allocated physical-register instructions into bytes.
// There is no code overlap between them.
//
// Reference: LLVM AArch64ISelLowering.cpp (tree-pattern matching + late combines)

//! AArch64 instruction selection: trust_ir SSA IR -> AArch64 MachIR with virtual registers.
//!
//! Phase 1 (this module): Walk trust_ir blocks in reverse postorder, match each
//! instruction bottom-up, emit AArch64 ISelInst with VRegs. This covers
//! arithmetic, comparisons, branches, calls, returns, loads, stores, and
//! constants.
//!
//! The ISel types (`ISelFunction`, `ISelInst`, `ISelBlock`, `ISelOperand`) are
//! ISel-specific intermediates, distinct from the canonical `trust_cg_ir::MachFunction`
//! / `MachInst` / `MachBlock` / `MachOperand` types. The pipeline adapter
//! (`isel_to_ir` in `trust-cg-codegen/pipeline.rs`) converts between them.
//!
//! Phase 2 (trust-cg-opt late combines): Address-mode formation, cmp+branch
//! fusing and csel/cset formation. Adjacent integer compare/branch pairs are
//! selected here when a complete function-use inventory proves the boolean
//! has no other consumer; wider combinations remain late machine combines.

